findings.suggestion:
Build into a private temporary directory and atomically rename it into place as the last step, or wrap the post-mkdir work in try/except that removes the partial output before re-raising, e.g.

    try:
        ...extract, generate, patch, write CONSUMER.json...
    except BaseException:
        shutil.rmtree(output, ignore_errors=True)
        raise

Replace the 3.9-only call with the equivalent membership test that works on older interpreters:

    if output == ROOT or ROOT in output.parents:
        raise ValueError('output must be outside the checkout')
